/Title (1. Top-Down Strategy:  Testing begins from the main modules such as the user interface and gradually moves to sub-modules like resume builder, career guidance, and interview preparation. 2. Bottom-Up Strategy:  Individual components like database connection, API functions, and authentication are tested first before integrating them into the main system. 3. Incremental Testing Strategy:  Modules are developed and tested step-by-step. Each new feature is tested after integration to ensure smooth performance. 4. System Testing Strategy:  After integrating all modules, the complete system is tested as a whole to verify overall functionality and performance.)
/Dest [39 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2846 0 R
>>
endobj
2858 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. Black Box Testing:  The system is tested without knowing internal code structure. Inputs and outputs are checked for correctness, such as login validation and career suggestions. 2. White Box Testing:  Internal code structure is tested to verify logic, loops, database queries, and API functions in Node.js backend.)
