/Title (1. Technical Feasibility : The system is technically feasible as it uses technologies like Node.js, Express, and databases such as MySQL or MongoDB. These technologies are widely available, easy to use, and well-supported. The AI features such as skill analysis and recommendations can be implemented using basic algorithms and APIs. 2. Economic Feasibility : The system is cost-effective because it uses open-source tools and software. There is no need for expensive hardware or paid licenses. Development and maintenance costs are low, making it affordable for students and small organizations. 3. Operational Feasibility : The system is user-friendly and easy to operate. Users can easily register, enter their details, and get career suggestions without any technical knowledge. The interface is simple, which ensures smooth interaction and usability. 4. Time Feasibility : The project can be completed within the given time frame. The modules can be developed step-by-step, making it manageable and efficient to implement within academic deadlines.)
